{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouping state is stored on the table using the following shape:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export type GroupingState = string[]\n\nexport type GroupingTableState = {\n  grouping: GroupingState\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"aggregation-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aggregation Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following aggregation functions are built-in to the table core:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sum"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sums the values of a group of rows"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"min"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finds the minimum value of a group of rows"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finds the maximum value of a group of rows"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"extent"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finds the minimum and maximum values of a group of rows"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mean"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finds the mean/average value of a group of rows"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"median"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finds the median value of a group of rows"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unique"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finds the unique values of a group of rows"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"uniqueCount"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finds the number of unique values of a group of rows"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"count"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Calculates the number of rows in a group"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every grouping function receives:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function to retrieve the leaf values of the groups rows"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function to retrieve the immediate-child values of the groups rows"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"and should return a value (usually primitive) to build the aggregated row model."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the type signature for every aggregation function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export type AggregationFn<TData extends AnyData> = (\n  getLeafRows: () => Row<TData>[],\n  getChildRows: () => Row<TData>[]\n) => any","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"using-aggregation-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using Aggregation Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aggregation functions can be used/referenced/defined by passing the following to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnDefinition.aggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" that references a built-in aggregation function"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" that references a custom aggregation functions provided via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions.aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function directly provided to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnDefinition.aggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The final list of aggregation functions available for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnDef.aggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":" use the following type:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export type AggregationFnOption<TData extends AnyData> =\n  | 'auto'\n  | keyof AggregationFns\n  | BuiltInAggregationFn\n  | AggregationFn<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-def-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Def Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"aggregationfn","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"aggregationFn?: AggregationFn | keyof AggregationFns | keyof BuiltInAggregationFns","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The aggregation function to use with this column."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" referencing a "},{"type":"link","href":"#aggregation-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"built-in aggregation function"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"link","href":"#aggregation-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"custom aggregation function"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"aggregatedcell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"}]},{"type":"code","value":"aggregatedCell?: Renderable<\n  {\n    table: Table<TData>\n    row: Row<TData>\n    column: Column<TData>\n    cell: Cell<TData>\n    getValue: () => any\n    renderValue: () => any\n  }\n>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The cell to display each row for the column if the cell is an aggregate. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object with the context of the cell and should return the property type for your adapter (the exact type depends on the adapter being used)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enablegrouping","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableGrouping"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableGrouping?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/disables grouping for this column."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getgroupingvalue","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGroupingValue"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getGroupingValue?: (row: TData) => any","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Specify a value to be used for grouping rows on this column. If this option is not specified, the value derived from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accessorKey"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accessorFn"},{"type":"text","value":" will be used instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"aggregationfn-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"aggregationFn?: AggregationFnOption<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The resolved aggregation function for the column."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcangroup","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCanGroup"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getCanGroup: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether or not the column can be grouped."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getisgrouped","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsGrouped"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsGrouped: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether or not the column is currently grouped."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getgroupedindex","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGroupedIndex"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getGroupedIndex: () => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the index of the column in the grouping state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"togglegrouping","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toggleGrouping"}]},{"type":"code","value":"toggleGrouping: () => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Toggles the grouping state of the column."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"gettogglegroupinghandler","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getToggleGroupingHandler"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getToggleGroupingHandler: () => () => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a function that toggles the grouping state of the column. This is useful for passing to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClick"},{"type":"text","value":" prop of a button."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getautoaggregationfn","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAutoAggregationFn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getAutoAggregationFn: () => AggregationFn<TData> | undefined","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the automatically inferred aggregation function for the column."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getaggregationfn","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAggregationFn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getAggregationFn: () => AggregationFn<TData> | undefined","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the aggregation function for the column."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"row-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"groupingcolumnid","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupingColumnId"}]},{"type":"code","value":"groupingColumnId?: string","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If this row is grouped, this is the id of the column that this row is grouped by."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"groupingvalue","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupingValue"}]},{"type":"code","value":"groupingValue?: any","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If this row is grouped, this is the unique/shared value for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupingColumnId"},{"type":"text","value":" for all of the rows in this group."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getisgrouped-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsGrouped"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsGrouped: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether or not the row is currently grouped."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getgroupingvalue-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGroupingValue"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getGroupingValue: (columnId: string) => unknown","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the grouping value for any row and column (including leaf rows)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"aggregationfns","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"}]},{"type":"code","value":"aggregationFns?: Record<string, AggregationFn>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This option allows you to define custom aggregation functions that can be referenced in a column's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":" option by their key.\nExample:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"declare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface AggregationFns {\n    myCustomAggregation: AggregationFn<unknown>\n  }\n}\n\nconst column = columnHelper.data('key', {\n  aggregationFn: 'myCustomAggregation',\n})\n\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  columns: [column],\n  aggregationFns: {\n    myCustomAggregation: (columnId, leafRows, childRows) => {\n      // return the aggregated value\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"manualgrouping","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"manualGrouping"}]},{"type":"code","value":"manualGrouping?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables manual grouping. If this option is set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the table will not automatically group rows using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGroupedRowModel()"},{"type":"text","value":" and instead will expect you to manually group the rows before passing them to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side grouping and aggregation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ongroupingchange","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onGroupingChange"}]},{"type":"code","value":"onGroupingChange?: OnChangeFn<GroupingState>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If this function is provided, it will be called when the grouping state changes and you will be expected to manage the state yourself. You can pass the managed state back to the table via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions.state.grouping"},{"type":"text","value":" option."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enablegrouping-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableGrouping"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableGrouping?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/disables grouping for all columns."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getgroupedrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGroupedRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getGroupedRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model after grouping has taken place, but no further."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"groupedcolumnmode","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupedColumnMode"}]},{"type":"code","value":"groupedColumnMode?: false | 'reorder' | 'remove' // default: `reorder`","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouping columns are automatically reordered by default to the start of the columns list. If you would rather remove them or leave them as-is, set the appropriate mode here."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"setgrouping","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setGrouping"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setGrouping: (updater: Updater<GroupingState>) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sets or updates the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.grouping"},{"type":"text","value":" state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resetgrouping","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetGrouping"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resetGrouping: (defaultState?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resets the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"grouping"}]},{"type":"text","value":" state to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState.grouping"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" can be passed to force a default blank state reset to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[]"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getpregroupedrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPreGroupedRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getPreGroupedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model for the table before any grouping has been applied."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getgroupedrowmodel-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getGroupedRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getGroupedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model for the table after grouping has been applied."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cell-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getisaggregated","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsAggregated"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsAggregated: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether or not the cell is currently aggregated."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getisgrouped-3","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsGrouped"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsGrouped: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether or not the cell is currently grouped."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getisplaceholder","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsPlaceholder"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsPlaceholder: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether or not the cell is currently a placeholder."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"state","text":"State","level":2},{"id":"aggregation-functions","text":"Aggregation Functions","level":2},{"id":"using-aggregation-functions","text":"Using Aggregation Functions","level":4},{"id":"column-def-options","text":"Column Def Options","level":2},{"id":"aggregationfn","text":"aggregationFn","level":3},{"id":"aggregatedcell","text":"aggregatedCell","level":3},{"id":"enablegrouping","text":"enableGrouping","level":3},{"id":"getgroupingvalue","text":"getGroupingValue","level":3},{"id":"column-api","text":"Column API","level":2},{"id":"aggregationfn-2","text":"aggregationFn","level":3},{"id":"getcangroup","text":"getCanGroup","level":3},{"id":"getisgrouped","text":"getIsGrouped","level":3},{"id":"getgroupedindex","text":"getGroupedIndex","level":3},{"id":"togglegrouping","text":"toggleGrouping","level":3},{"id":"gettogglegroupinghandler","text":"getToggleGroupingHandler","level":3},{"id":"getautoaggregationfn","text":"getAutoAggregationFn","level":3},{"id":"getaggregationfn","text":"getAggregationFn","level":3},{"id":"row-api","text":"Row API","level":2},{"id":"groupingcolumnid","text":"groupingColumnId","level":3},{"id":"groupingvalue","text":"groupingValue","level":3},{"id":"getisgrouped-2","text":"getIsGrouped","level":3},{"id":"getgroupingvalue-2","text":"getGroupingValue","level":3},{"id":"table-options","text":"Table Options","level":2},{"id":"aggregationfns","text":"aggregationFns","level":3},{"id":"manualgrouping","text":"manualGrouping","level":3},{"id":"ongroupingchange","text":"onGroupingChange","level":3},{"id":"enablegrouping-2","text":"enableGrouping","level":3},{"id":"getgroupedrowmodel","text":"getGroupedRowModel","level":3},{"id":"groupedcolumnmode","text":"groupedColumnMode","level":3},{"id":"table-api","text":"Table API","level":2},{"id":"setgrouping","text":"setGrouping","level":3},{"id":"resetgrouping","text":"resetGrouping","level":3},{"id":"getpregroupedrowmodel","text":"getPreGroupedRowModel","level":3},{"id":"getgroupedrowmodel-2","text":"getGroupedRowModel","level":3},{"id":"cell-api","text":"Cell API","level":2},{"id":"getisaggregated","text":"getIsAggregated","level":3},{"id":"getisgrouped-3","text":"getIsGrouped","level":3},{"id":"getisplaceholder","text":"getIsPlaceholder","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## State\n\nGrouping state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport type GroupingState = string[]\n\nexport type GroupingTableState = {\n  grouping: GroupingState\n}\n```\n\n## Aggregation Functions\n\nThe following aggregation functions are built-in to the table core:\n\n- `sum`\n  - Sums the values of a group of rows\n- `min`\n  - Finds the minimum value of a group of rows\n- `max`\n  - Finds the maximum value of a group of rows\n- `extent`\n  - Finds the minimum and maximum values of a group of rows\n- `mean`\n  - Finds the mean/average value of a group of rows\n- `median`\n  - Finds the median value of a group of rows\n- `unique`\n  - Finds the unique values of a group of rows\n- `uniqueCount`\n  - Finds the number of unique values of a group of rows\n- `count`\n  - Calculates the number of rows in a group\n\nEvery grouping function receives:\n\n- A function to retrieve the leaf values of the groups rows\n- A function to retrieve the immediate-child values of the groups rows\n\nand should return a value (usually primitive) to build the aggregated row model.\n\nThis is the type signature for every aggregation function:\n\n```tsx\nexport type AggregationFn<TData extends AnyData> = (\n  getLeafRows: () => Row<TData>[],\n  getChildRows: () => Row<TData>[]\n) => any\n```\n\n#### Using Aggregation Functions\n\nAggregation functions can be used/referenced/defined by passing the following to `columnDefinition.aggregationFn`:\n\n- A `string` that references a built-in aggregation function\n- A `string` that references a custom aggregation functions provided via the `tableOptions.aggregationFns` option\n- A function directly provided to the `columnDefinition.aggregationFn` option\n\nThe final list of aggregation functions available for the `columnDef.aggregationFn` use the following type:\n\n```tsx\nexport type AggregationFnOption<TData extends AnyData> =\n  | 'auto'\n  | keyof AggregationFns\n  | BuiltInAggregationFn\n  | AggregationFn<TData>\n```\n\n## Column Def Options\n\n### `aggregationFn`\n\n```tsx\naggregationFn?: AggregationFn | keyof AggregationFns | keyof BuiltInAggregationFns\n```\n\nThe aggregation function to use with this column.\n\nOptions:\n\n- A `string` referencing a [built-in aggregation function](#aggregation-functions))\n- A [custom aggregation function](#aggregation-functions)\n\n### `aggregatedCell`\n\n```tsx\naggregatedCell?: Renderable<\n  {\n    table: Table<TData>\n    row: Row<TData>\n    column: Column<TData>\n    cell: Cell<TData>\n    getValue: () => any\n    renderValue: () => any\n  }\n>\n```\n\nThe cell to display each row for the column if the cell is an aggregate. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object with the context of the cell and should return the property type for your adapter (the exact type depends on the adapter being used).\n\n### `enableGrouping`\n\n```tsx\nenableGrouping?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables grouping for this column.\n\n### `getGroupingValue`\n\n```tsx\ngetGroupingValue?: (row: TData) => any\n```\n\nSpecify a value to be used for grouping rows on this column. If this option is not specified, the value derived from `accessorKey` / `accessorFn` will be used instead.\n\n## Column API\n\n### `aggregationFn`\n\n```tsx\naggregationFn?: AggregationFnOption<TData>\n```\n\nThe resolved aggregation function for the column.\n\n### `getCanGroup`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanGroup: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the column can be grouped.\n\n### `getIsGrouped`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsGrouped: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the column is currently grouped.\n\n### `getGroupedIndex`\n\n```tsx\ngetGroupedIndex: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the index of the column in the grouping state.\n\n### `toggleGrouping`\n\n```tsx\ntoggleGrouping: () => void\n```\n\nToggles the grouping state of the column.\n\n### `getToggleGroupingHandler`\n\n```tsx\ngetToggleGroupingHandler: () => () => void\n```\n\nReturns a function that toggles the grouping state of the column. This is useful for passing to the `onClick` prop of a button.\n\n### `getAutoAggregationFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetAutoAggregationFn: () => AggregationFn<TData> | undefined\n```\n\nReturns the automatically inferred aggregation function for the column.\n\n### `getAggregationFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetAggregationFn: () => AggregationFn<TData> | undefined\n```\n\nReturns the aggregation function for the column.\n\n## Row API\n\n### `groupingColumnId`\n\n```tsx\ngroupingColumnId?: string\n```\n\nIf this row is grouped, this is the id of the column that this row is grouped by.\n\n### `groupingValue`\n\n```tsx\ngroupingValue?: any\n```\n\nIf this row is grouped, this is the unique/shared value for the `groupingColumnId` for all of the rows in this group.\n\n### `getIsGrouped`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsGrouped: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the row is currently grouped.\n\n### `getGroupingValue`\n\n```tsx\ngetGroupingValue: (columnId: string) => unknown\n```\n\nReturns the grouping value for any row and column (including leaf rows).\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `aggregationFns`\n\n```tsx\naggregationFns?: Record<string, AggregationFn>\n```\n\nThis option allows you to define custom aggregation functions that can be referenced in a column's `aggregationFn` option by their key.\nExample:\n\n```tsx\ndeclare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface AggregationFns {\n    myCustomAggregation: AggregationFn<unknown>\n  }\n}\n\nconst column = columnHelper.data('key', {\n  aggregationFn: 'myCustomAggregation',\n})\n\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  columns: [column],\n  aggregationFns: {\n    myCustomAggregation: (columnId, leafRows, childRows) => {\n      // return the aggregated value\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### `manualGrouping`\n\n```tsx\nmanualGrouping?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables manual grouping. If this option is set to `true`, the table will not automatically group rows using `getGroupedRowModel()` and instead will expect you to manually group the rows before passing them to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side grouping and aggregation.\n\n### `onGroupingChange`\n\n```tsx\nonGroupingChange?: OnChangeFn<GroupingState>\n```\n\nIf this function is provided, it will be called when the grouping state changes and you will be expected to manage the state yourself. You can pass the managed state back to the table via the `tableOptions.state.grouping` option.\n\n### `enableGrouping`\n\n```tsx\nenableGrouping?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables grouping for all columns.\n\n### `getGroupedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetGroupedRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model after grouping has taken place, but no further.\n\n### `groupedColumnMode`\n\n```tsx\ngroupedColumnMode?: false | 'reorder' | 'remove' // default: `reorder`\n```\n\nGrouping columns are automatically reordered by default to the start of the columns list. If you would rather remove them or leave them as-is, set the appropriate mode here.\n\n## Table API\n\n### `setGrouping`\n\n```tsx\nsetGrouping: (updater: Updater<GroupingState>) => void\n```\n\nSets or updates the `state.grouping` state.\n\n### `resetGrouping`\n\n```tsx\nresetGrouping: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the **grouping** state to `initialState.grouping`, or `true` can be passed to force a default blank state reset to `[]`.\n\n### `getPreGroupedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPreGroupedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table before any grouping has been applied.\n\n### `getGroupedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetGroupedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table after grouping has been applied.\n\n## Cell API\n\n### `getIsAggregated`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsAggregated: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the cell is currently aggregated.\n\n### `getIsGrouped`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsGrouped: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the cell is currently grouped.\n\n### `getIsPlaceholder`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsPlaceholder: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the cell is currently a placeholder.","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Grouping APIs\nid: grouping\n---\n\n## State\n\nGrouping state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport type GroupingState = string[]\n\nexport type GroupingTableState = {\n  grouping: GroupingState\n}\n```\n\n## Aggregation Functions\n\nThe following aggregation functions are built-in to the table core:\n\n- `sum`\n  - Sums the values of a group of rows\n- `min`\n  - Finds the minimum value of a group of rows\n- `max`\n  - Finds the maximum value of a group of rows\n- `extent`\n  - Finds the minimum and maximum values of a group of rows\n- `mean`\n  - Finds the mean/average value of a group of rows\n- `median`\n  - Finds the median value of a group of rows\n- `unique`\n  - Finds the unique values of a group of rows\n- `uniqueCount`\n  - Finds the number of unique values of a group of rows\n- `count`\n  - Calculates the number of rows in a group\n\nEvery grouping function receives:\n\n- A function to retrieve the leaf values of the groups rows\n- A function to retrieve the immediate-child values of the groups rows\n\nand should return a value (usually primitive) to build the aggregated row model.\n\nThis is the type signature for every aggregation function:\n\n```tsx\nexport type AggregationFn<TData extends AnyData> = (\n  getLeafRows: () => Row<TData>[],\n  getChildRows: () => Row<TData>[]\n) => any\n```\n\n#### Using Aggregation Functions\n\nAggregation functions can be used/referenced/defined by passing the following to `columnDefinition.aggregationFn`:\n\n- A `string` that references a built-in aggregation function\n- A `string` that references a custom aggregation functions provided via the `tableOptions.aggregationFns` option\n- A function directly provided to the `columnDefinition.aggregationFn` option\n\nThe final list of aggregation functions available for the `columnDef.aggregationFn` use the following type:\n\n```tsx\nexport type AggregationFnOption<TData extends AnyData> =\n  | 'auto'\n  | keyof AggregationFns\n  | BuiltInAggregationFn\n  | AggregationFn<TData>\n```\n\n## Column Def Options\n\n### `aggregationFn`\n\n```tsx\naggregationFn?: AggregationFn | keyof AggregationFns | keyof BuiltInAggregationFns\n```\n\nThe aggregation function to use with this column.\n\nOptions:\n\n- A `string` referencing a [built-in aggregation function](#aggregation-functions))\n- A [custom aggregation function](#aggregation-functions)\n\n### `aggregatedCell`\n\n```tsx\naggregatedCell?: Renderable<\n  {\n    table: Table<TData>\n    row: Row<TData>\n    column: Column<TData>\n    cell: Cell<TData>\n    getValue: () => any\n    renderValue: () => any\n  }\n>\n```\n\nThe cell to display each row for the column if the cell is an aggregate. If a function is passed, it will be passed a props object with the context of the cell and should return the property type for your adapter (the exact type depends on the adapter being used).\n\n### `enableGrouping`\n\n```tsx\nenableGrouping?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables grouping for this column.\n\n### `getGroupingValue`\n\n```tsx\ngetGroupingValue?: (row: TData) => any\n```\n\nSpecify a value to be used for grouping rows on this column. If this option is not specified, the value derived from `accessorKey` / `accessorFn` will be used instead.\n\n## Column API\n\n### `aggregationFn`\n\n```tsx\naggregationFn?: AggregationFnOption<TData>\n```\n\nThe resolved aggregation function for the column.\n\n### `getCanGroup`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanGroup: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the column can be grouped.\n\n### `getIsGrouped`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsGrouped: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the column is currently grouped.\n\n### `getGroupedIndex`\n\n```tsx\ngetGroupedIndex: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the index of the column in the grouping state.\n\n### `toggleGrouping`\n\n```tsx\ntoggleGrouping: () => void\n```\n\nToggles the grouping state of the column.\n\n### `getToggleGroupingHandler`\n\n```tsx\ngetToggleGroupingHandler: () => () => void\n```\n\nReturns a function that toggles the grouping state of the column. This is useful for passing to the `onClick` prop of a button.\n\n### `getAutoAggregationFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetAutoAggregationFn: () => AggregationFn<TData> | undefined\n```\n\nReturns the automatically inferred aggregation function for the column.\n\n### `getAggregationFn`\n\n```tsx\ngetAggregationFn: () => AggregationFn<TData> | undefined\n```\n\nReturns the aggregation function for the column.\n\n## Row API\n\n### `groupingColumnId`\n\n```tsx\ngroupingColumnId?: string\n```\n\nIf this row is grouped, this is the id of the column that this row is grouped by.\n\n### `groupingValue`\n\n```tsx\ngroupingValue?: any\n```\n\nIf this row is grouped, this is the unique/shared value for the `groupingColumnId` for all of the rows in this group.\n\n### `getIsGrouped`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsGrouped: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the row is currently grouped.\n\n### `getGroupingValue`\n\n```tsx\ngetGroupingValue: (columnId: string) => unknown\n```\n\nReturns the grouping value for any row and column (including leaf rows).\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `aggregationFns`\n\n```tsx\naggregationFns?: Record<string, AggregationFn>\n```\n\nThis option allows you to define custom aggregation functions that can be referenced in a column's `aggregationFn` option by their key.\nExample:\n\n```tsx\ndeclare module '@tanstack/table-core' {\n  interface AggregationFns {\n    myCustomAggregation: AggregationFn<unknown>\n  }\n}\n\nconst column = columnHelper.data('key', {\n  aggregationFn: 'myCustomAggregation',\n})\n\nconst table = useReactTable({\n  columns: [column],\n  aggregationFns: {\n    myCustomAggregation: (columnId, leafRows, childRows) => {\n      // return the aggregated value\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### `manualGrouping`\n\n```tsx\nmanualGrouping?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables manual grouping. If this option is set to `true`, the table will not automatically group rows using `getGroupedRowModel()` and instead will expect you to manually group the rows before passing them to the table. This is useful if you are doing server-side grouping and aggregation.\n\n### `onGroupingChange`\n\n```tsx\nonGroupingChange?: OnChangeFn<GroupingState>\n```\n\nIf this function is provided, it will be called when the grouping state changes and you will be expected to manage the state yourself. You can pass the managed state back to the table via the `tableOptions.state.grouping` option.\n\n### `enableGrouping`\n\n```tsx\nenableGrouping?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables grouping for all columns.\n\n### `getGroupedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetGroupedRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model after grouping has taken place, but no further.\n\n### `groupedColumnMode`\n\n```tsx\ngroupedColumnMode?: false | 'reorder' | 'remove' // default: `reorder`\n```\n\nGrouping columns are automatically reordered by default to the start of the columns list. If you would rather remove them or leave them as-is, set the appropriate mode here.\n\n## Table API\n\n### `setGrouping`\n\n```tsx\nsetGrouping: (updater: Updater<GroupingState>) => void\n```\n\nSets or updates the `state.grouping` state.\n\n### `resetGrouping`\n\n```tsx\nresetGrouping: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets the **grouping** state to `initialState.grouping`, or `true` can be passed to force a default blank state reset to `[]`.\n\n### `getPreGroupedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPreGroupedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table before any grouping has been applied.\n\n### `getGroupedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetGroupedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model for the table after grouping has been applied.\n\n## Cell API\n\n### `getIsAggregated`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsAggregated: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the cell is currently aggregated.\n\n### `getIsGrouped`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsGrouped: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the cell is currently grouped.\n\n### `getIsPlaceholder`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsPlaceholder: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether or not the cell is currently a placeholder."}
